    schema:description "Queensland Museum is the keeping place for the State Collection, a magnificent assemblage of 1.2 million cultural objects, natural history specimens and geological treasures and more than 14 million research items. Every year, we bring our collections to life through fieldwork, contemporary acquisitions, world-class research and a dynamic program of exhibitions, workshops, talks, lectures and major events including World Science Festival Brisbane." ;
    schema:name "Queensland Museum" ;
    schema:url "https://www.museum.qld.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:qnc
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The Queensland Naturalists’ Club Inc aims to study all branches of natural history, to encourage the preservation and protection of native flora and fauna and their environments. We also focus on publishing worthwhile observations on natural history and record club activities." ;
    schema:name "Queensland-Naturalists-Club" ;
    schema:url "https://www.qnc.org.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:qpws
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Part of Qld DETSI" ;
    schema:name "Queensland Parks and Wildlife Service" ;
    schema:url "https://parks.desi.qld.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:qsi
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The unit within Queensland Government that manages fundamental spatial information for the State." ;
    schema:name "Queensland Spatial Information" ;
    schema:url "https://qldspatial.information.qld.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:qvmag
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The Queen Victoria Museum and Art Gallery (QVMAG) is the cultural hub of Launceston and the leading destination for art, history and natural sciences in Northern Tasmania. " ;
    schema:name "Queen Victoria Museum and Art Gallery" ;
    schema:url "https://www.qvmag.tas.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:rbgdt
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """Botanic Gardens of Sydney encompasses three world-leading botanic gardens, Australia’s premier botanical research institute, and Sydney’s leading outdoor activation precinct.

As Australia’s oldest scientific institution, we are custodians of more than $1.2 billion in state significant cultural, heritage and botanical collections.

The Gardens are a leading entity within the tourism sector with a focus on engaging international, national and regional visitors.

Botanic Gardens of Sydney is the registered business name of the Royal Botanic Gardens and Domain Trust, which is constituted under the Royal Botanic Gardens and Domain Trust Act 1980.""" ;
    schema:name "Royal Botanic Gardens and Domain Trust" ;
    schema:url "https://www.service.nsw.gov.au/nswgovdirectory/royal-botanic-gardens-and-domain-trust-the"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:rbgv
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """Royal Botanic Gardens Victoria plays a leading role in the conservation of plants through biodiversity research, programs to protect rare and threatened plants, and the study of habitats. This work is supported by education and visitor programs about the importance of plants to life.

The Organization encompasses two diverse sites at Melbourne and Cranbourne and the State Botanical Collection housed at the National Herbarium of Victoria. Royal Botanic Gardens Victoria is managed by the Royal Botanic Gardens Board Victoria, which is responsible to the Minister for Environment.""" ;
    schema:name "Royal Botanic Gardens Victoria" ;
    schema:url "https://www.rbg.vic.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:reefcatchments
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Reef Catchments is the Natural Resource Management (NRM) Organization for the Mackay Whitsunday Isaac region. We facilitate change and work for long-term solutions to sustain, protect, and improve our region’s natural resources and environment, both now and into the future." ;
    schema:name "Reef Catchments" ;
    schema:url "https://reefcatchments.com.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:riotinto
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Rio Tinto Group is a British-Australian multinational company that is the world's second largest metals and mining corporation." ;
    schema:name "Rio Tinto" ;
    schema:url "https://www.riotinto.com"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:ror
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """ROR is a community-led project to develop an open, sustainable, usable, and unique identifier for every research organization in the world.

Between 2016 and 2018, a group of 17 organizations with a shared purpose invested their time and energy into an Org ID initiative, with the goal of defining requirements for an open, community-led organization identifier registry. The initiative was a transparent, accessible process to help work towards a better system for all of our communities.""" ;
    schema:name "Research Organization Registry Community" ;
    schema:url "https://ror.community/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:sa
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Formerly Department of Human Services" ;
    schema:name "Services Australia" ;
    schema:url "https://www.servicesaustralia.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:sa-dew
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The Department for Environment and Water (DEW) manages a complex portfolio of natural and built assets that are critical to the wellbeing and economic prosperity of all South Australians." ;
    schema:name "SA Department for Environment and Water" ;
    schema:url "https://www.environment.sa.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:sa-dewnr
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The South Australian Department for Environment, Water and Natural Resources (DEWNR) has changed its name. It is now the Department for Environment and Water (DEW). This name change occurred on March 22, 2018, according to State Records South Australia. The change was due to adjustments in ministerial portfolios and reporting lines. " ;
    schema:name "SA Department for Environment, Water and Natural Resources" ;
    schema:url "https://www.environment.sa.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:sa-herbarium
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """The State Herbarium of South Australia, sometimes called the South Australian Herbarium, and having the herbarium code, AD, is located in Adelaide, South Australia. It is one of several State and Commonwealth herbaria in Australia. The Department for Environment and Water is the state agency which is responsible for the Herbarium, but the Board of the Botanic Gardens and State Herbarium (established by an Act of Parliament, most recently the Botanic Gardens and State Herbarium Act 1978) is charged with its establishment and maintenance.

The herbarium is responsible for Electronic Flora of South Australia. It also produces the journal, Swainsona (formerly Journal of the Adelaide Botanic Gardens).""" ;
    schema:name "State Herbarium of South Australia" ;
    schema:url "https://www.botanicgardens.sa.gov.au/science/research/state-herbarium"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:sam
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The South Australian Museum has been committed to making Australia’s natural and cultural heritage accessible, engaging and fun for over 165 years. It is a place where families can learn and grow together. Today the Museum is one of the most visited museums in Australia and holds collections of national and international significance. It is a leader in remote and regional community engagement, and in Australian Aboriginal heritage and scientific research." ;
    schema:name "South Australian Museum" ;
    schema:url "https://www.samuseum.sa.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:scienceforwildlife
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """Science for Wildlife is a leading not-for-profit conservation Organization working to ensure a future for wildlife and the places they call home.

Bringing the best available science to wildlife conservation in Australia and beyond, through the creation and sharing of ecological knowledge we empower people to participate in conservation that has an on-the-ground, enduring impact. Working with iconic and important species in key areas, our research and conservation work is designed to bring broader ecosystem benefits, maximising gains for many other animals and their habitats. We work beyond fences, at a landscape scale to bring real world solutions to conservation challenges. Our work is highly regarded by government and industry partners and informs conservation policy and action both nationally and globally.""" ;
    schema:name "Science for Wildlife Ltd" ;
    schema:url "https://www.scienceforwildlife.org"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:scion
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Scion is a group of the New Zealand Institute for Bioeconomy Science" ;
    schema:name "Scion Crown Research Institute of NZ" ;
    schema:url "https://www.scionresearch.com"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:sfsgi
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """The Sydney Fungal Studies Group Incorporated (SFSGI) consists of mycological and other academics, students, and many other, non-academic but interested people of all age groups.

The SFSGI aims to advance the study of fungi at all levels, particularly the larger fungi, to educate people at all stages of skill and knowledge in the science of mycology, and to interact with groups and societies having mycological or closely related interests.

Membership is open to all, with the only requirements being that they are interested in contributing to the activities of the Group, subscribe to the aims of the Group, and that they respect the basic principles of nature conservation.""" ;
    schema:name "Sydney Fungal Studies Group" ;
    schema:url "https://www.sydneyfungalstudies.org.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:south-australia
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The State of South Australia" ;
    schema:name "State of South Australia" ;
    schema:url "https://www.sa.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:sunwater
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Sunwater is a Queensland-based water service provider, making the most of the available water supply for our agriculture, urban and industrial customers." ;
    schema:name "SunWater" ;
    schema:url "https://www.sunwater.com.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:surround
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """SURROUND is an Australian technology company that develops advanced software systems and supplies consulting services.

It is deeply involved with Linked Data in Australia.""" ;
    schema:name "SURROUND Pty Ltd" ;
    schema:url "https://surroundaustralia.com"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:swmc
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Skills and Workforce Ministerial Council" ;
    schema:name "Skills and Workforce Ministerial Council" ;
    schema:url "https://www.directory.gov.au/portfolios/employment-and-workplace-relations/department-employment-and-workplace-relations/skills-and-workforce-ministerial-council"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:tas-dnre
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "DNRE aims to deliver a sustainable Tasmania by protecting and enhancing Tasmania's cultural and natural values; facilitating productive and sustainable industries; and by promoting the sustainable use, presentation, and enjoyment of our cultural and natural values." ;
    schema:name "Tasmania Department of Natural Resources and Environment" ;
    schema:url "https://nre.tas.gov.au/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:tas-nre
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """The Department of Natural Resources and Environment Tasmania (NRE Tas) is responsible for delivering a sustainable Tasmania.
We deliver a sustainable Tasmania by protecting and enhancing Tasmania's cultural and natural values; facilitating productive and sustainable industries; and by promoting the sustainable use, presentation, and enjoyment of our cultural and natural values.""" ;
    schema:name "Department of Natural Resources and Environment Tasmania" ;
    schema:url "https://www.nre.tas.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:tas-nva
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The Natural Values Atlas provides authoritative and comprehensive information on Tasmania's natural values. It draws together, in one centralised location, data on Tasmanian flora and fauna including threatened species and weeds, as well as Tasmanian geodiversity and soil survey data. It also incorporates access to other essential data sets such as TASVEG and Threatened Native Vegetation Communities maps. The Natural Values Atlas allows observations of plants and animals from various sources to be viewed, recorded and analysed. It can be used to search for information on plant and animal species from Tasmania, Australia and can display maps showing their location and extent. The observations of plants and animals recorded in the Natural Values Atlas have been collected by a variety of custodians through general species surveys and projects undertaken for scientific research, environmental assessments, and other purposes throughout the State since the 1800's. The Natural Values Atlas provides data products such as the Natural Values Report, which brings several data sets together providing a resource that can be used for desktop assessments of natural values for specific areas. Core repository for biodiversity data held by the Tasmanian Government." ;
    schema:name "Tasmanian Natural Values Atlas Team" ;
    schema:url "https://www.naturalvaluesatlas.tas.gov.au/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:tc211
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The International Organization for Standardization's Technical Committee on \"Geographic information/Geomatics\", is charged with standardization in the field of digital geographic information." ;
    schema:name "ISO's Technical Committee 211" ;
    schema:url "https://www.iso.org/committee/54904.html"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:te-papa
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Te Papa is New Zealand's national museum, renowned for being bicultural, scholarly, innovative, and fun. Our success is built on our relationships with and our ability to represent our community." ;
    schema:name "Museum of New Zealand Te Papa Tongarewa" ;
    schema:url "https://www.tepapa.govt.nz"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:tern
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "TERN is Australia’s land ecosystem observatory." ;
    schema:name "Terrestrial Ecosystems Research Network" ;
    schema:url "https://www.tern.org.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:tmag
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """Tasmanian Museum and Art Gallery (TMAG) is Tasmania's leading natural and cultural heritage Organization. It is a combined museum, art gallery and herbarium which safeguards the physical evidence of Tasmania's natural and cultural heritage, and the cultural identity of Tasmanians.

TMAG is Australia's second-oldest museum and has its origins in the collections of Australia's oldest scientific society, the Royal Society of Tasmania, established in 1843.  The first permanent home of the museum opened on the corner of Argyle and Macquarie streets in 1863 and the museum has gradually expanded from this corner to occupy the entire city block.""" ;
    schema:name "Tasmanian Museum and Art Gallery" ;
    schema:url "https://www.tmag.tas.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:uadelaide
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The University of Adelaide is a public research university based in Adelaide, South Australia. Established in 1874, it is the third-oldest university in Australia." ;
    schema:name "University of Adelaide" ;
    schema:url "https://www.adelaide.edu.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:umweltaust
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "An employee-owned environmental and social professional services consultancy" ;
    schema:name "Umwelt Australia Pty Ltd" ;
    schema:url "https://www.umwelt.com.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:un
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The United Nations is an international organization founded in 1945. Currently made up of 193 Member States, the UN and its work are guided by the purposes and principles contained in its founding Charter." ;
    schema:name "United Nations" ;
    schema:url "https://www.un.org"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:und
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Notre Dame is a private Catholic University, extending from the West Coast of Australia in the beautiful and historic City of Fremantle, to the North-West town of Broome and across the continent to the heart of Sydney." ;
    schema:name "University of Notre Dame" ;
.

org:une
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The University of New England (UNE) is a public university in the New England region of the state of New South Wales, Australia. Founded in 1938, it was the first Australian university to be established outside of a state capital." ;
    schema:name "University of New England" ;
    schema:url "https://www.une.edu.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:unewcastle
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The University of Newcastle (UON), informally known as Newcastle University, is a public university in Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia. Established in 1965, it has a primary campus in the Newcastle suburb of Callaghan. The university also operates campuses in Ourimbah, Port Macquarie, Singapore, Newcastle CBD and Sydney CBD." ;
    schema:name "University of Newcastle" ;
    schema:url "https://www.newcastle.edu.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:unsw
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The University of New South Wales (UNSW) is a public research university based in Sydney, New South Wales, Australia. It is one of the founding members of Group of Eight, a coalition of Australian research-intensive universities." ;
    schema:name "University of New South Wales" ;
    schema:url "https://www.unsw.edu.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:uom
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The University of Melbourne is a public research university located in Melbourne, Australia. Founded in 1853, it is Australia's second oldest university and the oldest in Victoria. Its main campus is located in Parkville, an inner suburb north of Melbourne's central business district, with several other campuses located across Victoria." ;
    schema:name "University of Melbourne" ;
    schema:url "https://www.unimelb.edu.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:uq
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Ranked in the world's top 50, The University of Queensland is one of Australia's leading research and teaching institutions." ;
    schema:name "University of Queensland" ;
    schema:url "https://www.uq.edu.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:uts
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "UTS is a public university of technology defined by our support for the economic, social and cultural prosperity of our communities. We are measured by the success of our students, staff and partners and committed to research, innovation and the dissemination of knowledge of public value. We are, and always will be, an inclusive university." ;
    schema:name "University of Technology Sydney" ;
    schema:url "https://www.uts.edu.au/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:vic-atlas
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Provider of the Victorian Biodiverity Atlas. The VBA species observations are a foundation dataset that feeds into some of the many biodiversity tools used in everyday decision making - showing where wildlife is now and how this has changed over time.  This makes it a core input to the majority of the governments processes and programs that impact native species. Custodian organisation for biodiversity data held by the Victorian Government." ;
    schema:name "Victorian Biodiversity Atlas Team" ;
    schema:url "https://www.environment.vic.gov.au/biodiversity/victorian-biodiversity-atlas"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:vic-deeca
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "DEECA brings together Victoria’s energy, environment, water, agriculture, forestry, resources, climate action, and emergency management functions into a single department to maximise connections between the environment, community, industry and economy." ;
    schema:name "Victorian Department of Energy, Environment and Climate Action" ;
    schema:url "https://www.deeca.vic.gov.au/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:wa-bio
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The Biodiversity Information Office provides the Dandjoo platform. Dandjoo is Western Australia’s first whole-of-state biodiversity data platform, providing a way to discover and explore data from government, industry, and research providers. Custodian organisation for data sourced from within Western Australian environment-related sectors, including government, industry, research, and the community." ;
    schema:name "WA Biodiversity Information Office" ;
    schema:url "https://bio.wa.gov.au/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:wa-dbca
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "DBCA brings together the Parks and Wildlife Service, Botanic Gardens and Parks Authority, Zoological Parks Authority (Perth Zoo), Rottnest Island Authority, Conservation and Parks Commission, Swan River Trust (Swan Canning Riverpark) and Biodiversity and Conservation Science." ;
    schema:name "WA Department of Biodiversity, Conservation and Attractions" ;
    schema:url "https://www.dbca.wa.gov.au/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:wa-herbarium
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "The Western Australian Herbarium is responsible for the description and documentation of Western Australia's exceptional botanical species diversity." ;
    schema:name "Western Australian Herbarium" ;
    schema:url "https://www.dbca.wa.gov.au/science/research-tools-and-repositories/western-australian-herbarium"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:wabsi
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """A joint venture partnership with leading Western Australian science research Organizations, with multi-disciplinary research expertise.

An independent, collaboration mechanism to facilitate end user driven, relevant biodiversity science research.

Funded by the Western Australian Government’s Department of Jobs, Tourism, Science and Innovation.""" ;
    schema:name "Western Australian Biodiversity Science Institute" ;
    schema:url "https://wabsi.org.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:wam
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description """The Western Australian Museum is the State's premier cultural Organization, housing WA's scientific and cultural collection.

For over 120 years the Museum has been making the State's natural and social heritage accessible and engaging through research, exhibition and public programs.

Today, the Museum has seven public locations across the state - and a Collection and Research Centre that houses more than eight million objects.""" ;
    schema:name "Western Australian Museum" ;
    schema:url "https://visit.museum.wa.gov.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:western-shield
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "WA’s largest conservation program, Western Shield, works to manage introduced predators for native species conservation. Learn what animals are protected, where DBCA’s fauna recovery sites are located, and what management tools are used. " ;
    schema:name "Western Shield" ;
    schema:url "http://www.dbca.wa.gov.au/management/threat-management/invasive-animals/western-shield"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:wmbaustralia
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "Acquired by BTM in 2008" ;
    schema:name "WBM Oceanics Australia" ;
    schema:url "https://www.bmt.org/services/environment-solutions"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

org:wwf-australia
    a schema:Organization ;
    schema:description "At WWF-Australia we’ve been protecting nature’s wonders for more than 40 years. And now we’re working with communities, governments, companies and others not just to protect our natural world but to restore and regenerate it." ;
    schema:name "WWF Australia" ;
    schema:url "https://wwf.org.au"^^xsd:anyURI ;
.

